# Project Rules

When writing or editing code in this project, strictly follow these rules:

## 1. CSS Sizing
- ALWAYS use `rem` for sizing (e.g., margins, padding, font-size, width, height). Do not use `px`.

## 2. CSS Styling Approach
- ALWAYS use CSS Modules (`.module.css`) for component-specific styling.
- ALWAYS write Custom CSS. Do not use utility-class frameworks (like Tailwind CSS, Bootstrap, etc.) unless explicitly instructed otherwise.

## 3. Colors and Typography
- ALWAYS use the CSS variables defined in `/src/assets/css/index.css` for any colors and font-families. 
- Example: `color: var(--color-primary);` or `font-family: var(--font-primary);`.

## 4. General
- Maintain a clean and modular architecture.
- Ensure all styles are responsive and well-structured following the rules above.
